Clarity v0.5 (retrieval only) against v0.9 (tools and a loop), 120 cases

                      v0.5     v0.9  change, points
  composite           83%      83%      +0pt
  document            61%      96%     +35pt
  unanswerable        90%      75%     -15pt
  warehouse           20%      90%     +70pt
  overall             60%      91%     +31pt

  cases the newer system fixed : 45
  cases it broke               : 8
    tail-rotated-util, tail-termination, tail-target-miss, abstain-01,
    abstain-03, abstain-07, abstain-15, abstain-17

This is the comparison that survives contact with a manager, and the absolute
number is not it. Nobody can tell you whether 91% is good. Everybody can tell you
whether it beats what you had, by how much, and on which kinds of question.

Then read the second list. 45 cases got better and 8 got worse, and the
average contains both. 5 of the regressions are refusals: the older system
said it did not know, and the newer one, holding a warehouse and four tools,
found something to say instead.

That is a real cost of Part IV, it is invisible in a single number, and it is
the kind of thing an eval set exists to catch.
